This graph belongs to a linear, quadratic or exponential relationship. Identify its family and explain how you know.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=-3,xmax=3,ymin=-2,ymax=6,xtick={-2,-1,1,2},ytick={-1,1,2,3,4,5},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[curveblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth},domain=-2.7:2.7,samples=2] {2-x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

This graph belongs to a linear, quadratic or exponential relationship. Identify its family and explain how you know.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=-3,xmax=3,ymin=-4,ymax=4,xtick={-2,-1,1,2},ytick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[curveblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth},domain=-2.45:2.45,samples=100] {3-x*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Each graph belongs to a linear, quadratic or exponential relationship. Identify the family of A and B and explain how their shapes support your answers.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[name=graphA,width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=-3,xmax=3,ymin=-1,ymax=9,xtick={-2,-1,1,2},ytick={2,4,6,8},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},title={A},title style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[curveblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth},domain=-2.8:1.9,samples=100] {exp(x*ln(3))};
\end{axis}
\begin{axis}[at={(graphA.south west)},anchor=north west,yshift=-15mm,width=7cm,height=6cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={black,-{Stealth}},xmin=-3,xmax=3,ymin=-1,ymax=9,xtick={-2,-1,1,2},ytick={2,4,6,8},grid=major,grid style={gridgrey},scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,text=black},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},title={B},title style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={$x$},ylabel={$y$}]
\addplot[curveblue,thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth},domain=-1.9:2.8,samples=100] {exp(-x*ln(3))};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
